var o={name:`Plank`,description:`A static hold on the forearms. Works the core muscles and trunk stability.`,steps:[`Get into a forearm plank with your elbows under your shoulders.`,`Straighten your legs and align your body from your heels to your head.`,`Brace your abs and glutes.`,`Hold the position for the set time, breathing steadily.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder or lower back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Do not raise or lower your hips.`,`Do not hold your breath.`]};var r={name:`Superman`,description:`Lifting the arms and legs at the same time while lying face down. Works the back muscles and glutes.`,steps:[`Lie face down with your arms extended forward.`,`Lift your arms, chest and legs slightly off the floor at the same time.`,`Hold for 1–2 seconds.`,`Lower slowly.`],warnings:[`Do not lift abruptly or too high.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel lower back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Look down, with your neck in line with your spine.`,`Move smoothly, without jerking.`]};var s={name:`Burpee`,description:`A compound exercise: squat, plank, return and jump up. Builds overall endurance and works the whole body.`,steps:[`Squat down and place your hands on the floor.`,`Kick your feet back into a plank position.`,`Bring your feet back to your hands and stand up.`,`Do a small jump up with your arms overhead.`],warnings:[`Land softly and do not arch your lower back in the plank.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel joint or back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your body straight in the plank position.`,`Prioritize control over maximum speed.`]};var n={"bodyweight-squat":{name:`Bodyweight Squat`,description:`A basic squat without added weight. Works the quadriceps and glutes and builds control of movement in the knees and hips.`,steps:[`Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart.`,`Push your hips back and bend your knees, lowering down.`,`Lower to a comfortable depth, keeping your back straight.`,`Push through your feet and return to the starting position.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel knee pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Your knees move in the direction of your toes.`,`Do not lift your heels off the floor.`]},"split-squat":{name:`Split Squat`,description:`A squat in a wide stance. Works the quadriceps and glutes of each leg separately and improves balance.`,steps:[`Take a wide stance: one foot forward, the other back.`,`Lower straight down, bending both knees.`,`Rise up, pushing through your front foot.`,`Complete all reps, then switch legs.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel knee pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your torso upright.`,`Keep most of your weight on the front leg.`]},"reverse-lunge":{name:`Reverse Lunge`,description:`A lunge with a step back. Works the quadriceps and glutes and develops balance and coordination.`,steps:[`Stand tall with your feet hip-width apart.`,`Step back and lower down, bending both knees.`,`Push through your front foot and return to the starting position.`,`Alternate legs or complete all reps on one side.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel knee pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Step back in a controlled way, without jerking.`,`Keep your torso straight.`]},"glute-bridge":{name:`Glute Bridge`,description:`A hip raise from lying on your back. Works the glutes and the back of the thighs.`,steps:[`Lie on your back with your knees bent and feet on the floor.`,`Squeeze your glutes and lift your hips up.`,`Hold for a second at the top.`,`Slowly lower your hips to the floor.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel lower back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Do not arch your lower back at the top.`,`Press your heels into the floor.`]},"single-leg-glute-bridge":{name:`Single-Leg Glute Bridge`,description:`A harder variation of the glute bridge on one leg. Works the glutes and the back of the thighs and improves pelvic stability.`,steps:[`Lie on your back with your knees bent and feet on the floor.`,`Straighten one leg and lift it off the floor.`,`Lift your hips, pushing through the heel of the supporting leg.`,`Lower slowly; after the set, switch legs.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel lower back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your hips level and do not let them tilt.`,`Move slowly and with control.`]},"knee-push-up":{name:`Knee Push-Up`,description:`An easier push-up variation supported on the knees. Works the chest and triceps.`,steps:[`Kneel with your hands on the floor slightly wider than your shoulders.`,`Align your body from your knees to your head.`,`Bend your arms and lower your chest to the floor.`,`Push up and straighten your arms.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel wrist or shoulder pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your elbows at about 45° to your torso.`,`Do not let your lower back sag.`]},"push-up":{name:`Push-Up`,description:`The classic push-up from the floor. Works the chest, triceps and core stabilizers.`,steps:[`Get into a plank position with your hands slightly wider than your shoulders.`,`Align your body from your heels to your head.`,`Bend your arms and lower your chest to the floor.`,`Push up and straighten your arms.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel wrist or shoulder pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your abs and glutes tight.`,`Keep your elbows at about 45° to your torso.`]},"wall-push-up":{name:`Wall Push-Up`,description:`The easiest push-up variation, supported by a wall. Works the chest and triceps with minimal load.`,steps:[`Face a wall at arm's length.`,`Place your palms on the wall at shoulder height.`,`Bend your arms and bring your chest toward the wall.`,`Push back and return to the starting position.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your body straight like a board.`,`The farther your feet are from the wall, the harder it is.`]},"pike-push-up":{name:`Pike Push-Up`,description:`A push-up with raised hips that shifts the load to the shoulders. Works the deltoids and triceps.`,steps:[`Get into a plank position and raise your hips, forming an inverted "V".`,`Bend your arms and lower your head toward the floor between your hands.`,`Push up and straighten your arms.`,`Keep your hips high throughout the set.`],warnings:[`Lower slowly and do not rest your head on the floor.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder, wrist or neck pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Your elbows point back, not out to the sides.`,`Look at the floor between your hands.`]},plank:o,"side-plank":{name:`Side Plank`,description:`A static hold on your side, supported on the forearm. Works the obliques and core stabilizers.`,steps:[`Lie on your side with your elbow under your shoulder.`,`Stack your feet or place one in front of the other.`,`Lift your hips so your body forms a straight line.`,`Hold the position for the set time, then switch sides.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Do not let your hips sag.`,`Keep your neck in line with your body.`]},"dead-bug":{name:`Dead Bug`,description:`Alternately extending the opposite arm and leg while lying on your back. Works the deep core muscles and lower back control.`,steps:[`Lie on your back with your arms extended up and your legs bent at a right angle.`,`Slowly lower the opposite arm and leg toward the floor.`,`Return them to the starting position.`,`Repeat with the other arm and leg.`],warnings:[],techniqueNotes:[`Press your lower back into the floor.`,`Move slowly and exhale as you lower.`]},"bird-dog":{name:`Bird Dog`,description:`Alternately extending the opposite arm and leg from all fours. Works the core, glutes and coordination.`,steps:[`Get on your hands and knees, with your hands under your shoulders and knees under your hips.`,`Simultaneously extend one arm forward and the opposite leg back.`,`Hold for a second.`,`Return to the starting position and switch sides.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel wrist pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your back straight and do not arch.`,`Keep your hips parallel to the floor.`]},superman:r,"wall-sit":{name:`Wall Sit`,description:`A static seated hold with your back against a wall. Works the quadriceps and leg endurance.`,steps:[`Stand with your back to a wall, feet about half a meter away from it.`,`Slide your back down until your knees are bent at a comfortable angle.`,`Hold the position for the set time.`,`Slowly stand back up.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel knee pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your knees above your ankles, not past your toes.`,`Keep your back fully against the wall.`]},"jumping-jacks":{name:`Jumping Jacks`,description:`Jumps with the arms and legs spreading apart at the same time. Builds cardiovascular endurance and warms up the whole body.`,steps:[`Stand tall with your feet together and arms at your sides.`,`Jump your feet apart and raise your arms overhead.`,`Jump back to the starting position.`,`Continue at a steady pace for the set time.`],warnings:[`Land softly on the balls of your feet.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel knee or ankle pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your knees slightly bent when landing.`,`Breathe steadily.`]},"step-jacks":{name:`Step Jacks`,description:`A low-impact version of jumping jacks: step to the side while raising your arms overhead. Warms up the body and raises your heart rate without jumping.`,steps:[`Stand tall with your feet together and arms at your sides.`,`Step to the side and raise your arms overhead at the same time.`,`Bring your foot back in and lower your arms.`,`Alternate sides at a steady pace.`],warnings:[],techniqueNotes:[`Keep a pace that raises your heart rate moderately.`,`Step lightly.`]},"high-knees":{name:`High Knees`,description:`Running in place with high knee lifts. Builds cardiovascular endurance and foot speed.`,steps:[`Stand tall with your feet hip-width apart.`,`Start running in place, lifting your knees to about hip level.`,`Pump your arms in rhythm with your legs.`,`Continue for the set time.`],warnings:[`Land softly on the balls of your feet.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel knee or ankle pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your torso upright.`,`Do not lean back.`]},"march-in-place":{name:`March in Place`,description:`Walking in place with active arm movement. A light, low-impact cardio exercise for warming up and raising your heart rate.`,steps:[`Stand tall with your elbows bent.`,`Lift your knees one at a time, marching in place.`,`Swing your arms in rhythm with your steps.`,`Keep a steady pace for the set time.`],warnings:[],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your back straight.`,`To make it harder, lift your knees higher or speed up.`]},"mountain-climbers":{name:`Mountain Climbers`,description:`Alternately driving the knees toward the chest from a plank position. Builds endurance and works the core.`,steps:[`Get into a plank position with your hands under your shoulders.`,`Drive one knee toward your chest.`,`Return that leg back and drive the other knee in.`,`Alternate legs at a fast but controlled pace.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel wrist or shoulder pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Do not raise your hips high.`,`Keep your shoulders over your hands.`]},burpee:s,"squat-jump":{name:`Squat Jump`,description:`A squat with an explosive jump up. Builds leg strength and explosiveness.`,steps:[`Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart.`,`Squat down to a comfortable depth.`,`Jump up explosively.`,`Land softly and go straight into the next squat.`],warnings:[`Land softly with bent legs.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel knee or ankle pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Your knees move in the direction of your toes.`,`Land quietly and with control.`]},"cat-cow":{name:`Cat-Cow`,description:`Smoothly alternating between rounding and arching the back from all fours. Improves spinal mobility.`,steps:[`Get on your hands and knees with your hands under your shoulders.`,`As you inhale, arch your back and lift your gaze.`,`As you exhale, round your back and lower your head.`,`Repeat smoothly with your breathing rhythm.`],warnings:[`Move within a comfortable range and stop if you feel pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`The movement flows from the pelvis to the head.`,`Do not rush.`]},"kneeling-hip-flexor-stretch":{name:`Kneeling Hip Flexor Stretch`,description:`A stretch for the front of the thigh in a kneeling lunge position. Improves hip mobility.`,steps:[`Kneel on one knee with the other leg in front, bent at a right angle.`,`Squeeze the glute of the kneeling leg.`,`Gently shift your hips forward until you feel a stretch.`,`Hold the position for the set time, then switch legs.`],warnings:[`Put something soft under your knee; stop if you feel pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Do not arch your lower back.`,`The stretch should be moderate, without pain.`]},"arm-circles":{name:`Arm Circles`,description:`Circular rotations with straight arms. Warms up the shoulder joints and improves their mobility.`,steps:[`Stand tall and extend your arms out to the sides.`,`Make small circles forward with your arms.`,`Gradually increase the size of the circles.`,`Switch direction halfway through the time.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your shoulders down, not reaching toward your ears.`,`Move smoothly.`]},"open-book-rotation":{name:`Open Book Rotation`,description:`A thoracic spine rotation while lying on your side. Improves mobility of the upper back and shoulders.`,steps:[`Lie on your side with your knees bent and arms extended in front of you.`,`Sweep your top arm in an arc to the opposite side, rotating your chest.`,`Follow your hand with your eyes.`,`Return your arm back; after the set, switch sides.`],warnings:[`Move within a comfortable range and stop if you feel pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your knees together on the floor.`,`Breathe calmly.`]},"goblet-squat":{name:`Goblet Squat`,description:`A squat holding a dumbbell or kettlebell at your chest. Works the quadriceps and glutes and helps you keep your torso upright.`,steps:[`Hold a dumbbell or kettlebell upright at your chest.`,`Stand with your feet slightly wider than your shoulders.`,`Squat down, keeping your chest lifted.`,`Stand up, pushing through your feet.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel knee or back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Your elbows move between your knees.`,`Keep your back straight throughout the movement.`]},"dumbbell-romanian-deadlift":{name:`Dumbbell Romanian Deadlift`,description:`A forward bend with dumbbells, driven by hip movement. Works the hamstrings and glutes.`,steps:[`Stand tall with dumbbells in front of your thighs.`,`Slightly bend your knees and push your hips back.`,`Lower the dumbbells along your legs until you feel a stretch in the back of your thighs.`,`Return up, driving your hips forward.`],warnings:[`Do not round your back; choose a weight you can handle with good form.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel lower back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your back straight and the dumbbells close to your legs.`,`The movement comes from the hips, not the back.`]},"one-arm-dumbbell-row":{name:`One-Arm Dumbbell Row`,description:`Rowing a dumbbell to your waist in a bent-over position with hand support. Works the back muscles and biceps.`,steps:[`Lean forward, bracing your free hand on your thigh or a stable support.`,`Pick up the dumbbell with your arm straight under your shoulder.`,`Pull the dumbbell to your waist, driving your elbow back.`,`Lower slowly; after the set, switch arms.`],warnings:[`Keep your back straight; stop if you feel lower back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Do not rotate your torso during the pull.`,`Squeeze your shoulder blade toward your spine.`]},"dumbbell-floor-press":{name:`Dumbbell Floor Press`,description:`Pressing dumbbells up while lying on the floor with a limited range of motion. Works the chest and triceps.`,steps:[`Lie on your back with your knees bent and dumbbells in your hands at your chest.`,`Press the dumbbells up over your chest.`,`Lower slowly until your upper arms touch the floor.`,`Repeat the press.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your elbows at about 45° to your torso.`,`Lower the dumbbells with control, without slamming them on the floor.`]},"dumbbell-bench-press":{name:`Dumbbell Bench Press`,description:`Pressing dumbbells up while lying on a flat bench. Works the chest and triceps.`,steps:[`Lie on the bench with your feet on the floor and dumbbells at your chest.`,`Press the dumbbells up over your chest.`,`Slowly lower them to chest level.`,`Repeat the press.`],warnings:[`Choose a weight you can lower with control.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your shoulder blades pulled together and pressed into the bench.`,`Do not bounce the dumbbells off your chest.`]},"incline-dumbbell-press":{name:`Incline Dumbbell Press`,description:`Pressing dumbbells while lying on a bench with the backrest raised. Works the upper chest and front delts.`,steps:[`Set the bench back to a moderate incline.`,`Sit on the bench with your back pressed against it and dumbbells at your chest.`,`Press the dumbbells up over your upper chest.`,`Slowly lower and repeat.`],warnings:[`Make sure the bench back is securely locked.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your shoulder blades pulled together and pressed into the bench.`,`Move with control through the full range of motion.`]},"dumbbell-shoulder-press":{name:`Dumbbell Shoulder Press`,description:`Pressing dumbbells overhead while standing. Works the deltoids and triceps.`,steps:[`Stand tall with dumbbells at shoulder level.`,`Brace your abs and glutes.`,`Press the dumbbells up overhead.`,`Slowly lower to shoulder level.`],warnings:[`Do not arch your lower back during the press.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder, neck or back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your ribs down and your torso stable.`,`Do not tilt your head back.`]},"dumbbell-reverse-lunge":{name:`Dumbbell Reverse Lunge`,description:`A lunge with a step back, holding dumbbells. Works the quadriceps and glutes with added resistance.`,steps:[`Stand tall with dumbbells in your lowered hands.`,`Step back and lower down, bending both knees.`,`Push through your front foot and return to the starting position.`,`Alternate legs or complete all reps on one side.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel knee pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your torso upright.`,`Keep your shoulders down and the dumbbells from swinging.`]},"farmer-carry":{name:`Farmer's Carry`,description:`Walking with dumbbells or kettlebells in your lowered hands. Works the core, grip and overall stability.`,steps:[`Pick up dumbbells or kettlebells in both hands.`,`Stand tall with your shoulders down and back.`,`Walk with short, even steps for the set time.`,`Carefully set the weight down on the floor.`],warnings:[`Lift and lower the weight with a straight back.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel back or wrist pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Do not lean toward the side of the weight.`,`Keep your abs braced.`]},"kettlebell-swing":{name:`Kettlebell Swing`,description:`A dynamic kettlebell swing driven by hip movement. Builds power in the glutes and hamstrings, plus endurance.`,steps:[`Stand with your feet slightly wider than your shoulders and the kettlebell in front of you.`,`Hinge forward with a straight back and swing the kettlebell back between your legs.`,`Snap your hips forward so the kettlebell rises to chest level.`,`Let the kettlebell swing down and repeat the movement.`],warnings:[`Make sure there are no people or objects around you.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel lower back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`The movement comes from the hips; your arms just hold the kettlebell.`,`Keep your back straight at the bottom.`]},"kettlebell-deadlift":{name:`Kettlebell Deadlift`,description:`Lifting a kettlebell from the floor, driven by hip movement. Works the glutes and hamstrings and teaches proper lifting technique.`,steps:[`Stand over the kettlebell with your feet hip-width apart.`,`Push your hips back, bend your knees and grab the handle.`,`Stand up, driving your hips forward.`,`Lower the kettlebell to the floor with the same movement.`],warnings:[`Do not round your back as you lift.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel lower back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your back straight and eyes forward.`,`The kettlebell moves close to your body.`]},"band-pull-apart":{name:`Band Pull-Apart`,description:`Stretching a resistance band with straight arms in front of your chest. Works the upper back muscles and rear delts.`,steps:[`Hold the band in both hands at shoulder width in front of your chest.`,`Spread your arms out to the sides, stretching the band.`,`Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the end point.`,`Slowly return your arms to the starting position.`],warnings:[`Check the band for damage before the exercise.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your shoulders down and do not raise them to your ears.`,`Keep your arms almost straight throughout the movement.`]},"band-row":{name:`Band Row`,description:`Rowing an anchored resistance band to your waist. Works the back muscles and biceps.`,steps:[`Anchor the band at waist level to a secure support.`,`Hold the ends and step back until there is tension.`,`Pull your hands to your waist, driving your elbows back.`,`Slowly return your hands forward.`],warnings:[`Make sure the anchor is secure and the band is not damaged.`],techniqueNotes:[`Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the end point.`,`Keep your torso still and do not lean back.`]},"band-lat-pulldown":{name:`Band Lat Pulldown`,description:`Pulling a band anchored overhead down to your chest. Works the lats and biceps.`,steps:[`Anchor the band overhead to a secure support.`,`Hold the ends with your arms extended up.`,`Pull your elbows down to your sides, bringing your hands toward your chest.`,`Slowly return your hands up.`],warnings:[`Make sure the overhead anchor is secure and the band is not damaged.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Lower your shoulder blades before pulling.`,`Do not swing your torso.`]},"pull-up":{name:`Pull-Up`,description:`Pulling your body up on a bar to chin level. Works the back muscles and biceps.`,steps:[`Grip the bar slightly wider than your shoulders.`,`Hang with straight arms, with your shoulder blades pulled down.`,`Pull up until your chin is above the bar.`,`Slowly lower down to straight arms.`],warnings:[`Use only a securely mounted bar.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder or wrist pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Do not swing or jerk.`,`Lower with control.`]},"dead-hang":{name:`Dead Hang`,description:`A static hang from a bar with straight arms. Strengthens your grip and shoulder girdle muscles.`,steps:[`Grip the bar at shoulder width.`,`Carefully hang with straight arms.`,`Hold the position for the set time, breathing steadily.`,`Carefully step down to the floor.`],warnings:[`Use only a securely mounted bar.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder or wrist pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Engage your shoulders slightly; do not hang passively.`,`Do not swing.`]},"hanging-knee-raise":{name:`Hanging Knee Raise`,description:`Pulling your knees to your chest while hanging from a bar. Works the abs and grip.`,steps:[`Hang from the bar with straight arms.`,`Brace your abs and pull your knees to your chest.`,`Hold for a second.`,`Slowly lower your legs without swinging.`],warnings:[`Use only a securely mounted bar.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder or lower back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Move without jerking or swinging.`,`Slightly curl your pelvis at the top.`]},"jump-rope":{name:`Jump Rope`,description:`Rhythmic jumps over a rope. Builds cardiovascular endurance, coordination and calf strength.`,steps:[`Hold the rope handles with the rope behind your heels.`,`Turn the rope with your wrists.`,`Do small jumps as the rope passes under your feet.`,`Keep a steady rhythm for the set time.`],warnings:[`Jump low and land softly on the balls of your feet.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel knee or ankle pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your elbows close to your body.`,`Keep your knees slightly bent.`]},"step-up":{name:`Step-Up`,description:`Stepping up onto a stable platform, alternating legs. Works the quadriceps and glutes.`,steps:[`Stand in front of the platform.`,`Place your whole foot on it with one leg.`,`Stand up, pushing through the leg on the platform.`,`Slowly step down and repeat; switch legs after the set.`],warnings:[`Make sure the platform is stable and does not slide.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel knee pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Do not push off with the bottom leg.`,`Your knee moves in the direction of your toes.`]},"barbell-back-squat":{name:`Barbell Back Squat`,description:`A squat with a barbell on your upper back. Builds strength in the quadriceps, glutes and the whole body.`,steps:[`Place the barbell on your upper back and unrack it.`,`Step back with your feet shoulder-width apart or slightly wider.`,`Squat to a comfortable depth, keeping your back straight.`,`Stand up and, after the set, return the barbell to the rack.`],warnings:[`Set the rack safety pins and use a weight you can control.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel knee, back or shoulder pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Brace your core before each rep.`,`Your knees move in the direction of your toes.`]},"barbell-deadlift":{name:`Barbell Deadlift`,description:`Lifting a barbell from the floor to a standing position. Builds strength in the hamstrings, glutes and back.`,steps:[`Stand with the bar over the middle of your feet.`,`Push your hips back, bend your knees and grip the bar.`,`Stand up, keeping the bar close to your legs.`,`Lower the barbell to the floor with the same movement.`],warnings:[`Do not round your back; use a weight you can control.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel lower back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your back straight and your core braced.`,`Push the floor away with your legs rather than pulling with your back.`]},"cardio-machine-intervals":{name:`Cardio Machine Intervals`,description:`Interval work on a stationary bike, elliptical or other cardio machine. Builds cardiovascular endurance.`,steps:[`Warm up for a few minutes at an easy pace.`,`Increase the pace or resistance for the set interval time.`,`During rest, keep moving at an easy pace.`,`Repeat the interval the set number of times.`],warnings:[`Read the machine's instructions before using it.`,`Slow down or stop if you feel dizzy or any pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`The intensity should feel hard but controlled.`,`Keep an upright posture.`]},"jump-rope-boxer-step":{name:`Jump Rope Boxer Step`,description:`Low jumps over a rope, shifting your weight from one foot to the other. Easier than two-footed jumps.`,steps:[`Hold the rope handles with the rope behind your heels.`,`Turn the rope with your wrists.`,`Lightly shift your weight from one foot to the other, as if stepping in place.`,`Keep a steady rhythm for the set time.`],warnings:[`Jump low and land softly on the balls of your feet.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel ankle pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Jump only a few centimeters off the floor.`,`Keep your elbows close to your body.`]},"jump-rope-side-to-side":{name:`Jump Rope Side-to-Side`,description:`Two-footed jumps with a small shift left and right. Adds load to the calves and trains coordination.`,steps:[`Hold the rope handles with your feet together.`,`Jump over the rope, shifting slightly to the left.`,`On the next jump, shift to the right.`,`Keep the rhythm and land softly.`],warnings:[`Make sure you have enough space and the surface is not slippery.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel knee or ankle pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep the shift small, no wider than your feet.`,`Keep your knees slightly bent.`]},"jump-rope-high-knees":{name:`Jump Rope High Knees`,description:`Running in place over a rope with knee lifts. An intense cardio exercise for endurance.`,steps:[`Hold the rope handles with the rope behind your heels.`,`Run in place, passing the rope under your foot on every step.`,`Lift your knees to hip level.`,`Keep the pace for the set time.`],warnings:[`Do this only after a warm-up.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel knee, hip or ankle pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your torso straight and do not lean back.`,`Land softly on the balls of your feet.`]},"lateral-step-up":{name:`Lateral Step-Up`,description:`Stepping up onto a platform sideways. Loads the glutes and thigh muscles from a different angle than a regular step-up.`,steps:[`Stand sideways to the platform with the near foot on it.`,`Straighten that leg as you step up onto the platform.`,`Lower back down with control.`,`Finish your sets on one leg, then switch legs.`],warnings:[`Make sure the platform is stable and does not slide.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel knee or hip pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`The supporting leg does the work; the other only touches down.`,`Do not let your knee cave inward.`]},"step-platform-push-up":{name:`Step Platform Push-Up`,description:`A push-up with your hands on a platform. An easier version of the classic push-up for beginners.`,steps:[`Place your hands on the platform slightly wider than your shoulders, with your body in a straight line.`,`Bend your elbows, lowering your chest to the platform.`,`Push up, straightening your arms.`,`Keep your core braced.`],warnings:[`The platform must be stable, preferably on a non-slip surface.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel wrist or shoulder pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Do not arch your lower back.`,`Keep your elbows at about 45° to your torso.`]},"step-platform-calf-raise":{name:`Step Platform Calf Raise`,description:`Calf raises from the edge of a platform for a bigger range of motion. Strengthens the calf muscles.`,steps:[`Stand on the edge of the platform on the balls of your feet, with your heels in the air.`,`Slowly lower your heels below the platform level.`,`Rise as high as you can onto your toes.`,`Repeat without jerking.`],warnings:[`Hold onto a wall or post for balance.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel ankle or Achilles tendon pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Move slowly: 2 seconds up, 2 seconds down.`,`Keep your knees almost straight.`]},"step-platform-reverse-lunge":{name:`Step Platform Reverse Lunge`,description:`Stepping back off a platform into a lunge. A bigger range of motion for the glutes and thighs.`,steps:[`Stand on the platform with your feet hip-width apart.`,`Step one leg back onto the floor.`,`Lower into a lunge, with your front foot staying on the platform.`,`Return to the starting position and switch legs.`],warnings:[`Make sure the platform is stable and does not slide.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel knee pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your torso upright.`,`Keep your front heel pressed into the platform.`]},"step-platform-taps":{name:`Step Platform Taps`,description:`Fast alternating taps on a platform with your feet. A light cardio exercise for warming up and endurance.`,steps:[`Stand in front of the platform.`,`Tap the platform with your right foot, then your left.`,`Move quickly and lightly, without stepping fully onto it.`,`Keep the rhythm for the set time.`],warnings:[`The platform must be stable.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel knee pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your back straight and your arms moving in rhythm.`,`Keep the movements light, without impact.`]},"bench-dip":{name:`Bench Dip`,description:`A triceps dip with your hands on a bench behind you.`,steps:[`Sit on the edge of the bench with your hands beside your hips.`,`Slide forward, supporting yourself with your hands on the bench.`,`Bend your elbows to about 90°.`,`Straighten your arms and return up.`],warnings:[`Do not lower too deep if you feel discomfort in your shoulders.`,`The bench must be stable.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder or wrist pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Your elbows point back, not out to the sides.`,`Do not raise your shoulders to your ears.`]},"bulgarian-split-squat":{name:`Bulgarian Split Squat`,description:`A single-leg squat with the rear foot on a bench. Heavily loads the glutes and thighs.`,steps:[`Stand with your back to a bench and place the top of one foot on it.`,`Lower down, bending the front leg.`,`Rise up, pushing through the heel of the front foot.`,`Complete all reps, then switch legs.`],warnings:[`The bench must be stable; set your distance so your knee does not go past your foot.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel knee or hip pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Lean your torso slightly forward.`,`Keep most of your weight on the front leg.`]},"bench-hip-thrust":{name:`Bench Hip Thrust`,description:`A hip raise with your shoulder blades resting on a bench. The main exercise for the glutes.`,steps:[`Sit on the floor with your back to a bench and your shoulder blades on the edge of the bench.`,`Bend your knees with your feet on the floor.`,`Lift your hips until your torso and thighs form one line.`,`Pause briefly and lower.`],warnings:[`The bench must not move; it is best against a wall.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel lower back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your chin slightly tucked toward your chest.`,`Do not arch your lower back at the top.`]},"chest-supported-dumbbell-row":{name:`Chest-Supported Dumbbell Row`,description:`Rowing dumbbells while lying chest-down on an incline bench. Takes load off the lower back and focuses it on the back muscles.`,steps:[`Lie chest-down on the bench with a dumbbell in each hand.`,`Pull the dumbbells toward the sides of your torso, squeezing your shoulder blades together.`,`Pause briefly.`,`Lower the dumbbells with control.`],warnings:[`The bench must be stable.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your head in line with your spine.`,`Do not swing your torso.`]},"kettlebell-single-arm-row":{name:`Kettlebell Single-Arm Row`,description:`Rowing a kettlebell in a bent-over position with your free hand supported. Strengthens the back and biceps.`,steps:[`Lean forward with a straight back, bracing your free hand on your thigh.`,`Pick up the kettlebell with the other hand.`,`Pull the kettlebell to your waist, squeezing your shoulder blade.`,`Lower the kettlebell slowly.`],warnings:[`Keep your back straight.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel lower back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Your elbow moves along your torso.`,`Look at the floor.`]},"kettlebell-overhead-press":{name:`Kettlebell Overhead Press`,description:`A standing single-arm kettlebell press. Strengthens the shoulders, triceps and core.`,steps:[`Lift the kettlebell to your shoulder with your elbow pressed against your body.`,`Brace your abs and glutes.`,`Straighten your arm up overhead.`,`Slowly return the kettlebell to your shoulder.`],warnings:[`Make sure there is enough space above you.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder, neck or lower back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Do not arch your lower back.`,`Keep your wrist straight, with the kettlebell resting on your forearm.`]},"kettlebell-halo":{name:`Kettlebell Halo`,description:`Circling a kettlebell around your head. Warms up the shoulders and works core stability.`,steps:[`Stand tall and hold the kettlebell upside down at your chest.`,`Pass the kettlebell around your head in one direction.`,`Return it to your chest.`,`Repeat in the other direction.`],warnings:[`Use a light kettlebell.`,`Hold the kettlebell firmly so you do not hit yourself.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder or neck pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your torso still; only your arms move.`,`Keep your elbows close to your head.`]},"kettlebell-sumo-deadlift":{name:`Kettlebell Sumo Deadlift`,description:`Lifting a kettlebell with a wide stance. Loads the glutes and inner thighs.`,steps:[`Stand with a wide stance, toes turned out, with the kettlebell between your feet.`,`Push your hips back and grab the kettlebell.`,`Stand up, pushing the floor away with your legs.`,`Slowly lower the kettlebell.`],warnings:[`Do not round your back.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel lower back or hip pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Your knees move in the direction of your toes.`,`Keep your back straight throughout the movement.`]},"kettlebell-reverse-lunge":{name:`Kettlebell Reverse Lunge`,description:`A reverse lunge with a kettlebell at your chest. Adds load to the legs and glutes.`,steps:[`Hold the kettlebell at your chest with both hands.`,`Step back and lower into a lunge.`,`Push through your front foot and return.`,`Switch legs.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel knee pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your torso upright.`,`Keep your front heel pressed into the floor.`]},"band-squat":{name:`Band Squat`,description:`A squat with a band under your feet. The band adds resistance as you stand up.`,steps:[`Stand on the middle of the band and hold the ends at shoulder level.`,`Squat down, pushing your hips back.`,`Stand up, straightening your legs.`,`Do not let go of the band abruptly.`],warnings:[`Check that the band is not damaged.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel knee pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your knees in the direction of your toes.`,`Keep your back straight.`]},"band-chest-press":{name:`Band Chest Press`,description:`Pressing a band out in front of you while standing. Works the chest and triceps without dumbbells.`,steps:[`Wrap the band behind your back below your shoulder blades, with the ends in your hands.`,`Bend your elbows, with your hands at chest level.`,`Extend your arms forward.`,`Slowly return.`],warnings:[`Check that the band is not damaged and sits securely behind your back.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your elbows slightly below shoulder level.`,`Keep your torso still.`]},"band-overhead-press":{name:`Band Overhead Press`,description:`Pressing a band up while standing on it. Strengthens the shoulders and triceps.`,steps:[`Stand on the band and hold the ends at shoulder level.`,`Straighten your arms up overhead.`,`Slowly lower them back to your shoulders.`,`Do not arch your lower back.`],warnings:[`Make sure there is enough space above you.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder or neck pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your abs braced.`,`Move your arms vertically.`]},"band-good-morning":{name:`Band Good Morning`,description:`Bending your torso forward with a straight back, with the band on your shoulders and under your feet. Teaches the hip hinge movement.`,steps:[`Stand on the band and place the other end across your shoulders.`,`Push your hips back, bending your torso forward with a straight back.`,`Lower until you feel a stretch in the back of your thighs.`,`Stand up, driving your hips forward.`],warnings:[`Do not round your back.`,`Check that the band is securely anchored.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel lower back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your knees slightly bent.`,`Look down and slightly forward.`]},"band-bicep-curl":{name:`Band Bicep Curl`,description:`A biceps curl with band resistance.`,steps:[`Stand on the band with the ends in your hands and palms facing forward.`,`Bend your elbows, raising your hands to your shoulders.`,`Pause briefly.`,`Slowly lower your hands.`],warnings:[`Check that the band is not damaged.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your elbows pressed to your sides.`,`Do not swing your torso.`]},"scapular-pull-up":{name:`Scapular Pull-Up`,description:`Raising and lowering the shoulder blades while hanging, without bending the arms. Prepares the shoulders for pull-ups.`,steps:[`Hang from the bar with straight arms.`,`Pull your shoulders down and squeeze your shoulder blades together, lifting your body a few centimeters.`,`Slowly return to the hang.`,`Do not bend your elbows.`],warnings:[`Use only a securely mounted bar.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder or wrist pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep the movement small, only in the shoulder blades.`,`Do not swing your body.`]},"negative-pull-up":{name:`Negative Pull-Up`,description:`Slowly lowering from the top position of a pull-up. Helps you learn to do pull-ups.`,steps:[`Stand on a chair and grip the bar with your chin above it.`,`Remove the support.`,`Lower slowly until your arms are straight (3–5 seconds).`,`Return to the chair and repeat.`],warnings:[`Use only a securely mounted bar.`,`Use a chair to get into the top position.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder or wrist pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Lower with control, without dropping.`,`Keep your shoulder blades pulled down.`]},"chin-up":{name:`Chin-Up`,description:`A pull-up with your palms facing you. Works the biceps harder than a regular pull-up.`,steps:[`Grip the bar with an underhand grip at shoulder width.`,`Pull up until your chin is above the bar.`,`Pause briefly.`,`Slowly lower into a hang.`],warnings:[`Use only a securely mounted bar.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder, elbow or wrist pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Do not swing.`,`Your elbows move down and toward your torso.`]},"hanging-leg-raise":{name:`Hanging Leg Raise`,description:`Raising straight legs while hanging from a bar. A harder version for the abs.`,steps:[`Hang from the bar.`,`Brace your abs and raise your straight legs to pelvis level.`,`Pause briefly.`,`Slowly lower your legs.`],warnings:[`Use only a securely mounted bar.`,`Do not swing; raise your legs slowly.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder or lower back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your pelvis slightly tucked.`,`No swinging of the body.`]},"dumbbell-lateral-raise":{name:`Dumbbell Lateral Raise`,description:`Raising dumbbells out to the sides to shoulder level. Builds the middle heads of the deltoids.`,steps:[`Stand tall with dumbbells at your sides.`,`Slightly bend your elbows and raise your arms out to the sides to shoulder level.`,`Slowly lower your arms.`,`Do not raise your shoulders to your ears.`],warnings:[`Choose light dumbbells.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder or neck pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your elbows slightly higher than your hands.`,`Keep your torso still.`]},"dumbbell-bicep-curl":{name:`Dumbbell Bicep Curl`,description:`The classic standing biceps curl.`,steps:[`Stand tall with dumbbells in your lowered hands and palms facing forward.`,`Bend your elbows, raising the dumbbells to your shoulders.`,`Pause briefly.`,`Slowly lower the dumbbells.`],warnings:[`Choose a weight that does not make you swing your torso.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your elbows pressed to your sides.`,`Do not lean back.`]},"dumbbell-overhead-triceps-extension":{name:`Dumbbell Overhead Triceps Extension`,description:`Extending your arms with a dumbbell behind your head. Isolates the triceps.`,steps:[`Stand tall and hold a dumbbell overhead with both hands.`,`Bend your elbows, lowering the dumbbell behind your head.`,`Straighten your arms up.`,`Keep your elbows close to your head.`],warnings:[`Hold the dumbbell with both hands.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder, elbow or neck pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Do not let your elbows flare out to the sides.`,`Keep your abs braced.`]},"dumbbell-sumo-squat":{name:`Dumbbell Sumo Squat`,description:`A squat with a wide stance and a dumbbell between your legs. Emphasizes the glutes and inner thighs.`,steps:[`Stand with a wide stance, toes turned out, holding a dumbbell low with both hands.`,`Squat down with your knees in the direction of your toes.`,`Stand up, pushing the floor away with your legs.`,`Keep your torso upright.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel knee or hip pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your back straight.`,`Do not let your knees cave inward.`]},"dumbbell-glute-bridge":{name:`Dumbbell Glute Bridge`,description:`A glute bridge with a dumbbell on your hips. Adds load to the glutes.`,steps:[`Lie on your back with your knees bent and a dumbbell on your hips.`,`Lift your hips, straightening your body into a line.`,`Pause briefly.`,`Lower slowly.`],warnings:[`Hold the dumbbell firmly.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel lower back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Do not arch your lower back.`,`Keep your heels pressed into the floor.`]},"dumbbell-bent-over-row":{name:`Dumbbell Bent-Over Row`,description:`Rowing two dumbbells to your waist in a bent-over position. Strengthens the back and biceps.`,steps:[`Lean forward with a straight back and dumbbells in your lowered hands.`,`Pull the dumbbells toward your sides, squeezing your shoulder blades together.`,`Pause briefly.`,`Slowly lower the dumbbells.`],warnings:[`Keep your back straight.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel lower back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your knees slightly bent.`,`Drive your elbows along your torso.`]},"towel-row":{name:`Towel Row`,description:`Pulling your body toward a towel anchored to a secure support. Works the back muscles and biceps without equipment.`,steps:[`Wrap a strong towel around a secure support at waist level and hold both ends.`,`Lean back with straight arms, with your feet closer to the support.`,`Pull your chest toward your hands, driving your elbows back.`,`Slowly straighten your arms and return to the starting position.`],warnings:[`Anchor the towel only to a secure support: a sturdy post, a railing or the handle of a closed door that opens away from you.`,`Check that the towel is strong and does not slip out of your hands.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your body straight from head to heels.`,`The closer your feet are to the support, the harder the exercise.`]},"inverted-table-row":{name:`Inverted Table Row`,description:`A horizontal pull-up lying under a sturdy table. Works the back muscles, biceps and rear delts.`,steps:[`Lie on your back under the table so that your chest is under the edge of the tabletop.`,`Grip the edge of the tabletop at shoulder width.`,`Brace your abs and glutes and pull your chest toward the edge of the table.`,`Slowly lower, fully straightening your arms.`],warnings:[`Use only a heavy, stable table that will not tip over and will hold your weight.`,`Grip the edge of the tabletop, not glass or complicated parts.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your body straight from shoulders to heels, with your hips not sagging.`,`To make it easier, bend your knees and place your feet on the floor.`]},"prone-y-t-w-raise":{name:`Prone Y-T-W Raise`,description:`Arm raises in three positions while lying face down. Works the upper back and shoulder blade stabilizers.`,steps:[`Lie face down with your forehead above the floor and your arms extended forward.`,`Raise your arms in a Y shape, hold for a second and lower.`,`Spread your arms out to the sides in a T shape, raise and lower.`,`Bend your elbows into a W shape, squeeze your shoulder blades together, then raise and lower your arms. That is one rep.`],warnings:[`Do not tilt your head back.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder or neck pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`The movement comes from the shoulder blades, not the lower back.`,`Keep your thumbs pointing up.`]},"reverse-snow-angel":{name:`Reverse Snow Angel`,description:`A smooth arm movement from your hips to your head while lying face down. Works the upper back and shoulder mobility.`,steps:[`Lie face down with your arms along your body and palms toward your thighs.`,`Lift your arms off the floor and squeeze your shoulder blades together.`,`Slowly sweep your arms in an arc out to the sides all the way up to your head.`,`Return your arms to your thighs along the same path, without touching the floor.`],warnings:[`Do not tilt your head back.`,`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder or neck pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your arms slightly above the floor the whole time.`,`Do not arch your lower back; keep your glutes tight.`]},"leg-press":{name:`Leg Press`,description:`Pressing a platform away with your legs while seated. Works the quadriceps and glutes without loading the spine, and is good for beginners.`,steps:[`Sit in the machine with your lower back pressed against the backrest and your feet on the platform at shoulder width.`,`Release the safety catches and slowly bend your knees to a comfortable depth.`,`As you exhale, straighten your legs without fully locking your knees.`,`Return the safety catches to their place when you finish the set.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel knee pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Your lower back stays against the backrest.`,`Your knees move in the direction of your toes.`]},"machine-chest-press":{name:`Machine Chest Press`,description:`Pressing handles away from your chest while seated. Safely teaches the pressing movement and works the chest, shoulders and triceps.`,steps:[`Adjust the seat so the handles are at mid-chest level.`,`Grip the handles and press your shoulder blades against the backrest.`,`As you exhale, extend your arms forward without fully locking your elbows.`,`Slowly return the handles, feeling a stretch in your chest.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Do not raise your shoulders to your ears.`]},"machine-shoulder-press":{name:`Machine Shoulder Press`,description:`A vertical seated press on a machine. Works the shoulders and triceps with back support.`,steps:[`Adjust the seat so the handles are at shoulder level.`,`Press your back against the backrest and grip the handles.`,`As you exhale, extend your arms up.`,`Slowly lower the handles to shoulder level.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Do not arch your lower back.`]},"seated-cable-row":{name:`Seated Cable Row`,description:`A horizontal pull on a cable handle. Works the back and rear delts and teaches you to squeeze your shoulder blades together.`,steps:[`Sit down, place your feet on the footrests and grip the handle with a straight back.`,`Pull the handle toward your stomach, squeezing your shoulder blades together.`,`Pause briefly at the end point.`,`Slowly return your arms forward without rounding your back.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel lower back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Your torso stays almost still.`,`Your elbows move along your body.`]},"lat-pulldown-machine":{name:`Lat Pulldown`,description:`Pulling a wide handle down to your chest while seated. Prepares you for pull-ups and works the lats.`,steps:[`Secure your thighs under the pads and grip the handle wider than your shoulders.`,`Lean back slightly and pull the handle to your upper chest.`,`Squeeze your shoulder blades together and pause briefly.`,`Slowly return the handle up.`],warnings:[],techniqueNotes:[`Pull with your elbows, not your hands.`]},"leg-curl-machine":{name:`Leg Curl Machine`,description:`An isolated leg curl, lying or seated. Works the hamstrings.`,steps:[`Adjust the pad so it sits above your heels.`,`As you exhale, bend your legs, pulling your heels toward your glutes.`,`Pause briefly at the top.`,`Slowly straighten your legs.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel knee pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Your hips stay on the bench.`]},"leg-extension-machine":{name:`Leg Extension Machine`,description:`An isolated seated leg extension. Works the quadriceps.`,steps:[`Adjust the backrest and the pad above your shins.`,`As you exhale, straighten your legs.`,`Pause briefly at the top.`,`Slowly lower your legs.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel knee pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your movements smooth, without jerking.`]},"cable-triceps-pushdown":{name:`Cable Triceps Pushdown`,description:`Pushing your arms down on a high cable. Isolates the triceps.`,steps:[`Stand in front of the cable and grip the handle with your elbows pressed to your sides.`,`As you exhale, straighten your arms downward.`,`Pause briefly at the bottom.`,`Slowly return the handle to chest level.`],warnings:[],techniqueNotes:[`Your elbows do not move.`]},"cable-biceps-curl":{name:`Cable Biceps Curl`,description:`A standing curl at a low cable. Isolates the biceps.`,steps:[`Stand in front of the low cable and grip the handle with your palms facing up.`,`As you exhale, bend your arms toward your shoulders.`,`Pause briefly at the top.`,`Slowly straighten your arms.`],warnings:[],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your elbows pressed to your sides and your torso still.`]},"cable-face-pull":{name:`Cable Face Pull`,description:`Pulling a rope handle to face level. Strengthens the rear delts and the muscles between the shoulder blades, and is good for posture.`,steps:[`Attach the rope to the cable at face level and step back one pace.`,`Pull the rope toward your face, flaring your elbows out to the sides.`,`Squeeze your shoulder blades together and pause briefly.`,`Slowly return your arms forward.`],warnings:[],techniqueNotes:[`Use a light weight and keep the movement controlled.`]},"cable-woodchop":{name:`Cable Woodchop`,description:`A diagonal torso rotation with a cable handle. Works the obliques and teaches you to transfer force through the core.`,steps:[`Stand sideways to the cable and grip the handle with both hands.`,`Pull the handle diagonally downward, rotating your torso.`,`Keep your arms almost straight and rotate through your rib cage.`,`Slowly return the handle and repeat, then switch sides.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel lower back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Move your torso, not just your arms.`]},"barbell-bench-press":{name:`Barbell Bench Press`,description:`The classic barbell press on a flat bench. The main exercise for the chest, shoulders and triceps.`,steps:[`Lie on the bench with your feet on the floor, your shoulder blades squeezed together and your eyes under the bar.`,`Unrack the barbell and lower it to mid-chest.`,`As you exhale, press the barbell up until your arms are straight.`,`Rack the barbell when you finish the set.`],warnings:[`Do not bench press in the gym without a spotter, and stop the exercise if you feel shoulder pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Have a spotter or use safety stops.`,`Keep your wrists above your elbows.`]},"barbell-bent-over-row":{name:`Barbell Bent-Over Row`,description:`Rowing a barbell to your stomach in a bent-over position. Works the whole back, rear delts and biceps.`,steps:[`Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart and grip the bar slightly wider than your shoulders.`,`Lean forward with a straight back and slightly bent knees.`,`Pull the barbell to your lower stomach.`,`Slowly lower the barbell without rounding your back.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel lower back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your back straight throughout the movement.`]},"barbell-overhead-press":{name:`Barbell Overhead Press`,description:`A standing barbell press overhead. Builds strength in the shoulders and upper back and requires a stable core.`,steps:[`Hold the barbell at collarbone level with a grip slightly wider than your shoulders.`,`Brace your abs and glutes and, as you exhale, press the barbell up.`,`At the top, your head moves slightly forward, with the bar over the middle of your feet.`,`Slowly lower the barbell to your collarbones.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel shoulder or lower back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Do not arch your lower back.`]},"barbell-romanian-deadlift":{name:`Barbell Romanian Deadlift`,description:`A deadlift with nearly straight legs. Works the hamstrings and glutes and teaches the hip hinge movement.`,steps:[`Stand holding the barbell with your knees slightly bent.`,`Push your hips back, guiding the barbell along your legs.`,`Lower it below your knees, keeping your back straight.`,`As you exhale, return to the starting position, driving your hips forward.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel lower back pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`The movement comes from the hips, not the back.`]},"treadmill-incline-walk":{name:`Treadmill Incline Walk`,description:`Brisk walking on a treadmill with an incline. Low-impact cardio for endurance and the legs.`,steps:[`Set an incline of 4–8% and a comfortable brisk walking speed.`,`Keep your torso upright and do not lean on the handrails.`,`Walk at a steady pace for the needed time.`,`At the end, reduce the speed and incline to recover.`],warnings:[],techniqueNotes:[`Your breathing stays steady; you should be able to speak in short phrases.`]},"easy-run-intervals":{name:`Easy Run Intervals`,description:`Alternating easy running and walking. Builds heart and breathing endurance without sudden strain.`,steps:[`Warm up for a minute with a brisk walk.`,`Run at a comfortable pace for the set time.`,`Switch to walking to recover.`,`Repeat the alternation for the number of sets.`],warnings:[`Stop running if you feel ankle or knee pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`The pace lets you breathe through your nose or speak in short phrases.`]},"sprint-intervals":{name:`Sprint Intervals`,description:`Short bursts at full speed with full rest. Build power and speed endurance.`,steps:[`Warm up well and run a few light accelerations.`,`Accelerate to about 90% of your maximum speed.`,`After the sprint, walk back and recover fully.`,`Repeat for the number of sets.`],warnings:[`Do not do this on a slippery surface, and stop the exercise if you feel knee or ankle pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Lean your torso forward and drive your arms.`]},"brisk-walk-intervals":{name:`Brisk Walk Intervals`,description:`Alternating brisk and easy walking outdoors. Suitable for getting started and for recovery.`,steps:[`Walk at an easy pace for a minute to warm up.`,`Walk briskly, swinging your bent arms.`,`Switch to an easy pace to recover.`,`Repeat the alternation.`],warnings:[],techniqueNotes:[`At a brisk pace, your breathing is quicker, but you can still talk.`]},"walking-lunge":{name:`Walking Lunge`,description:`Lunges moving forward. Work the legs and glutes and teach balance.`,steps:[`Stand tall with your hands on your hips or at your sides.`,`Take a big step forward and lower down, bending both knees to 90°.`,`Push through your front foot and bring your back foot up to the front step.`,`Continue, alternating legs.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel knee pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your front knee above your ankle.`]},"bear-crawl":{name:`Bear Crawl`,description:`Moving on all fours with your knees raised. Strengthens the shoulders, core and legs and develops coordination.`,steps:[`Get on your hands and feet with your knees 5 cm above the ground.`,`Move the opposite arm and leg forward at the same time.`,`Keep your back flat and your hips low.`,`Move for the set time, then crawl backward the same way.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel wrist pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your movements slow and controlled.`]},"broad-jump":{name:`Standing Broad Jump`,description:`An explosive forward jump from two feet. Builds leg power and coordination.`,steps:[`Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart and swing your arms back.`,`Push off, swinging your arms forward, and jump as far as you can.`,`Land softly on bent knees.`,`Stop, regain your balance and repeat.`],warnings:[`Do not do this on a slippery surface, and stop the exercise if you feel knee pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Land softly on your whole foot.`]},"skater-jumps":{name:`Skater Jumps`,description:`Lateral jumps from one leg to the other. Train balance, legs and endurance.`,steps:[`Stand on one leg with the other leg swept back.`,`Jump sideways onto the other leg, swinging your arms.`,`Pause briefly, holding your balance.`,`Jump back and continue for the set time.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel knee or ankle pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Land softly, with your knee behind your toes.`]},"shuttle-run":{name:`Shuttle Run`,description:`Running between two points with a change of direction. Builds reaction speed and endurance.`,steps:[`Mark two points 3 m apart.`,`Run to the second point and touch the ground with your hand.`,`Quickly turn around and run back.`,`Repeat for the set time.`],warnings:[`Do not do this on a slippery surface.`],techniqueNotes:[`Turn with your knees bent and without crossing your feet.`]},"stair-climb":{name:`Stair Climb`,description:`A fast climb up stairs or a steep slope. Cardio and a workout for the legs and glutes.`,steps:[`Stand at the bottom of the stairs or slope.`,`Climb at a brisk pace, placing your whole foot on each step.`,`Climb for the set time, then descend slowly.`,`Repeat for the number of sets.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel knee pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Descend calmly, holding the handrail if needed.`]},"park-bench-step-up":{name:`Park Bench Step-Up`,description:`Stepping up onto a stable bench on one leg. Works the quadriceps and glutes.`,steps:[`Check that the bench is stable and stand in front of it.`,`Place one foot on the bench and step up, straightening your leg.`,`Step down slowly, controlling the movement.`,`Finish the set and switch legs.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel knee pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Push through the leg on the bench rather than pushing off the ground.`]},"park-bench-incline-push-up":{name:`Park Bench Incline Push-Up`,description:`A push-up with your hands on a bench. An easier variation for the chest, shoulders and triceps.`,steps:[`Place your palms on the edge of a stable bench with your body in one line.`,`Bend your elbows and lower your chest to the bench.`,`As you exhale, push up until your arms are straight.`,`Keep your core braced throughout the movement.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel wrist pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your elbows at about 45° to your torso.`]},"australian-pull-up":{name:`Australian Pull-Up`,description:`Pulling your body up to a low bar while lying under it. Works the back and biceps and is easier than a pull-up.`,steps:[`Stand under a low, sturdy bar and grip it wider than your shoulders.`,`Extend your body into a straight line with your heels on the ground.`,`Pull your chest to the bar, squeezing your shoulder blades together.`,`Slowly lower to almost straight arms.`],warnings:[`Make sure the bar is sturdy, and stop the exercise if you feel shoulder pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Keep your body straight and do not let your hips sag.`]},"outdoor-plank-shoulder-taps":{name:`Plank Shoulder Taps`,description:`A plank with alternating taps to the shoulder. Works the core and shoulder stability.`,steps:[`Get into a high plank with your feet slightly wider than your shoulders.`,`Tap your left shoulder with your right hand without rocking your hips.`,`Return your hand and tap with the other one.`,`Continue alternating for the set time.`],warnings:[`Stop the exercise if you feel wrist pain.`],techniqueNotes:[`Your hips barely move.`]}};export{s as burpee,n as default,o as plank,r as superman};